# The Vercel deployment is static. The PHP API deploys to Render.
#
# This is a security control, not just noise: a static host has no PHP runtime,
# so every .php file uploaded here would be served as plain text, turning the
# whole API into source disclosure. Keep the PHP tree on the Render side only.

# API source, as a directory pattern so it covers everything beneath it.
*.php
docker/
.vercel/

# Server and deployment config: not needed to serve static files, and
# render.yaml plus the Dockerfile describe the other half of the system.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.htaccess
render.yaml

# Secrets and machine-specific local state.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vs/
.neon
neon.ts
package.json
package-lock.json
skills-lock.json

# Agent tooling. Gitignored, but .vercelignore replaces .gitignore for the
# upload, so it has to be repeated here or ~300KB of internal skill docs get
# published alongside the app.
.agents/

# Repo metadata that is not needed to serve the site.
.gitattributes

# Documentation and the schema. schema.sql in particular is the full table
# layout, which is not something to publish next to a live API.
README.md
schema.sql

# .env.example is deliberately NOT excluded: it is a tracked template with
# every value empty, and it documents the variables the API expects.
